<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.worldline.reads ~ render the fork graph of conversation turns

`selector` names the run or handle to walk. `sensorium` names the sensorium; absent, memory.

The address stands ''candidate'' until the operator reads the landing's list. The MCP seat runs this act in its own process: the vessel's `call` binds the params against this carrier's live `#/takes` and answers `handler/seat` with the bound params, and the seat runs them (`act(address="lar:///sense.worldline.reads", args={…})`).

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ selector · sensorium

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`selector` params=`takes/word ~ the run or handle to walk`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`sensorium` params=`takes/word ~ the sensorium by name; absent, memory`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ seat

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`seat` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ the vessel verbs the seat's handler reaches check the face's cap and the asker's hand themselves; a hand act refuses a seat by its own code`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

